      "id": "user-1786579167377",
      "role": "user",
      "isShownToUser": true,
      "content": "Build a post-apocalyptic loot auto-battler. It's fully text-based, mobile-first but responsive enough to work with mouse and keyboard on desktop too. The player scavenges ruined locations for gear, equips it into a backpack, and fights auto-resolved battles where item stats and combos determine the outcome — no manual combat input, the build does the fighting.\n\nFor feel, borrow from Scavenge Wars the location-based looting loop: visiting a ruined location carries a real chance of an ambush that costs you items or energy, not just a guaranteed reward. Borrow from Backpack Brawl the equip mechanic: items slot into a limited backpack, and their combined properties (damage type, defense, rarity) roll up into an overall power level — call it \"weight class\" — that roughly predicts who wins a matchup, the way a heavier loadout usually beats a scrappier one.\n\nScreens: Loot Locations, Backpack/Inventory, Arena, and a light Trader Outpost. Everything is text and UI, no camera or spatial rendering. Items and log entries are colored strictly by rarity tier — common, uncommon, rare, epic, legendary, and a distinct color reserved for one-of-a-kind items — so the player can read power level at a glance.\n\nThe v1 loop: player taps a loot location card (trigger). The game rolls the location event — either an item find or an ambush (action). On a find, the item drops into loose inventory; on a lost ambush, an item or energy is removed (result), logged as a colored text entry with a short flavor line (feedback). The player then drags or taps found items into backpack slots, watching their weight class total update live as they swap gear. From there they enter the Arena and pick an opponent from a pool of saved player builds — async, no live matchmaking, just battling against a snapshot of how someone else's backpack was equipped — with a handful of seeded NPC \"veteran\" builds mixed in early so the pool isn't empty on day one. The battle auto-resolves with a quick text log of exchanges, and the winner earns currency plus a chance at an item reward roughly matched to the tiers involved. Returning to the game after time away shows a short popup: how many battles happened passively against the player's own build while they were gone, wins, losses, and currency gained. The Trader Outpost is present but light for v1: simple buy and sell of items, plus one or two basic consumables like an energy-restoring recovery juice — no research system, no deep pricing economy yet.\n\nTone is dry post-apocalyptic scavenger humor — a legendary-tier item can absolutely be a paperclip. A good session looks like: loot a location, find something usable, adjust the backpack, run a couple of arena battles, and walk away with more currency or gear than you started with, watching your weight class creep upward over several sessions. There's no game-over state — losing a fight or an ambush just costs items or currency and the loop continues.",
      "timestamp": 1786579167377,
      "type": "text",
      "metadata": {}
    },
