    {
      "id": "1786580456694-1b04h6bx7",
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The game is built and compiles clean. Here's what's in:\n\n**Spore Run** — plague & rot, dry deadpan, text-based auto-battler\n\n**4 screens via bottom tab bar:**\n- **RUINS** — 8 scavengeable locations (Fungal Grove, Overgrown Hospital, Research Lab sublevel, etc.), each with energy cost, ambush chance, and rarity range. Loot events show item found or ambush loss as a modal with dry flavor text. Log panel at the bottom tracks recent events colored by type/rarity.\n- **LOADOUT** — 8 backpack slots displayed as a grid. Tap inventory item to equip to first free slot; tap equipped item to unequip. Weight class updates live with bio (×3 = +15% WC) and hazmat (×2 = +20 WC) combo callouts.\n- **ARENA** — 6 seeded NPC opponents from Patient Zero (WC 16) up to The Collector (WC 655+). Shows weight class differential per opponent. Auto-battles resolve with a ~5-line text log; winner earns scrip and 30% chance of an item.\n- **OUTPOST** — Random stock of 4 items + 2 always-available consumables (Recovery Juice restores energy, Scout's Map gives luck on next run). Sell loose inventory at 50% value.\n\n**Systems:**\n- 40 items across 6 rarity tiers (common → one-of-a-kind), plague-themed with dry descriptions. The Paperclip is legendary, as requested.\n- Energy regenerates 1 per 30 min offline; passive arena battles fire every 2 hours (max 5 per session). Welcome-back popup on return.\n- Full save persistence via RUN appStorage + localStorage fallback.\n- Analytics on every major action (loot visit, ambush, battle win/loss, buy, sell, consumable use).",
      "isShownToUser": true,
      "timestamp": 1786580473366,
      "type": "text",
      "metadata": {}
    },
